class flSnaps:
    """snap object constants

Snap Enum Namespace.

## What is flSnaps?

`flSnaps` is not a class you instantiate — it is a collection of enum dictionaries for all snap-related constants. Access them as `flSnaps.SnapMode`, `flSnaps.SnapLineFlags`, etc. Use these constants when reading or writing snap flags on guidelines and snap objects.

## flSnaps.SnapMode — How snap distance is calculated

| Key | Native value | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `NoMode` | `flSnaps::SnapMode::NoMode` | Snapping disabled. |
| `Point` | `flSnaps::SnapMode::Point` | Snap to a discrete point (node, anchor, etc.). |
| `BeamAll` | `flSnaps::SnapMode::BeamAll` | Snap using beam (alignment) projection in all directions. |
| `AllModes` | `flSnaps::SnapMode::AllModes` | All snap modes combined. |

## flSnaps.SnapLineFlags — Guideline type and behaviour flags

These bits describe what kind of guideline a snap line is and how it should behave.

| Key | Native value | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `ShortGuideline` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::ShortGuideline` | A bounded (non-infinite) guideline segment. |
| `NoOrdinates` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::NoOrdinates` | Native enum value. |
| `Vector` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::Vector` | A vector (angled) guideline. |
| `Horizontal` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::Horizontal` | This is a horizontal guideline (angle ≈ 0°). |
| `Vertical` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::Vertical` | This is a vertical guideline (angle ≈ 90°). |
| `HorzVert` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::HorzVert` | Horizontal or vertical. |
| `RoleOrdinates` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::RoleOrdinates` | Used as an ordinate reference. |
| `Basic` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::Basic` | A standard, non-specialised guideline. |
| `Auto` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::Auto` | This guideline was generated automatically. |
| `RoleView` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::RoleView` | Native enum value. |
| `Width` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::Width` | Represents a glyph advance-width reference. |
| `Coordinate` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::Coordinate` | Carries a numeric coordinate value. |
| `AbsoluteMarkersPos` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::AbsoluteMarkersPos` | Marker positions are absolute (not relative to the guideline). |
| `RoleMeasures` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::RoleMeasures` | Used for measurements (ruler). |
| `AscLine` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::AscLine` | An ascender reference line. |
| `DscLine` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::DscLine` | A descender reference line. |
| `NullLine` | `flSnaps::SnapLineFlags::NullLine` | A baseline (zero reference) line. |

## flSnaps.MarkerFlags — What a marker represents

| Key | Native value | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `FillsShape` | `flSnaps::MarkerFlags::FillsShape` | This marker fills (colours) the interior of the shape. |
| `LeftMetric` | `flSnaps::MarkerFlags::LeftMetric` | This marker is a left sidebearing reference. |
| `RightMetric` | `flSnaps::MarkerFlags::RightMetric` | This marker is a right sidebearing reference. |

## flSnaps.MarkerKey — Marker classification

| Key | Native value | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `UndefinedMarker` | `flSnaps::MarkerKey::UndefinedMarker` | Unclassified. |
| `HandMarker` | `flSnaps::MarkerKey::HandMarker` | Manually placed by the designer. |
| `AutoMarker` | `flSnaps::MarkerKey::AutoMarker` | Automatically detected. |
| `AnyKeyMarker` | `flSnaps::MarkerKey::AnyKeyMarker` | Wildcard — matches any marker type in queries. |

## Tutorial

```python
import fontlab as fl
from fontlab import flSnaps

# Print all available snap mode values:
print("SnapMode:", flSnaps.SnapMode)
print("MarkerFlags:", flSnaps.MarkerFlags)
print("MarkerKey:", flSnaps.MarkerKey)

# Read snap flags from a guideline:
font = fl.CurrentFont()
for gl in font.guidelines:
    flag = gl.snapFlag(0)   # role 0 = general snap
    is_vert = bool(flag & flSnaps.SnapLineFlags["Vertical"])
    is_horz = bool(flag & flSnaps.SnapLineFlags["Horizontal"])
    print(f"Guideline at {gl.centerPoint}: vert={is_vert}  horz={is_horz}")
